## Ver extensiones instaladas
```sql
SELECT * FROM pg_extension;
SELECT * FROM pg_available_extensions ORDER BY name;
```

## Instalar extensión
```sql
CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS nombre;
```

## Extensiones frecuentes

### uuid-ossp
Generar UUIDs:
```sql
CREATE EXTENSION 'uuid-ossp';
SELECT uuid_generate_v4();
```

### pgcrypto
Hashes y encryption:
```sql
CREATE EXTENSION pgcrypto;
SELECT crypt('password', gen_salt('bf'));   -- bcrypt
SELECT digest('data', 'sha256');
```

### pg_trgm (trigram search)
Búsqueda fuzzy y LIKE eficiente:
```sql
CREATE EXTENSION pg_trgm;

-- Índice para LIKE con wildcards
CREATE INDEX idx_users_name_trgm ON users USING GIN (name gin_trgm_ops);

-- Similaridad
SELECT name, similarity(name, 'jorge')
FROM users
WHERE name % 'jorge'   -- % = similar
ORDER BY similarity(name, 'jorge') DESC;
```

### unaccent
Quitar acentos:
```sql
CREATE EXTENSION unaccent;
SELECT unaccent('José García');   -- 'Jose Garcia'

-- Combinar con búsqueda
WHERE unaccent(nombre) ILIKE unaccent('%jose%')
```

### hstore
Key-value dentro de una columna:
```sql
CREATE EXTENSION hstore;

ALTER TABLE products ADD COLUMN attributes hstore;
UPDATE products SET attributes = 'color=>red, size=>M';

SELECT * FROM products WHERE attributes -> 'color' = 'red';
```

**Considerar JSONB en vez** para nuevos schemas.

### PostGIS (geoespacial)
```sql
CREATE EXTENSION postgis;

CREATE TABLE ubicaciones (
    id serial,
    nombre text,
    geom geometry(Point, 4326)
);

INSERT INTO ubicaciones (nombre, geom)
VALUES ('Bogotá', ST_SetSRID(ST_MakePoint(-74.08, 4.60), 4326));

-- Distancia
SELECT nombre, ST_Distance(
    geom::geography,
    ST_SetSRID(ST_MakePoint(-74.10, 4.65), 4326)::geography
) AS metros
FROM ubicaciones;
```

### pg_stat_statements
Ya cubierto — obligatorio en prod.

### tablefunc (pivot tables)
```sql
CREATE EXTENSION tablefunc;
SELECT * FROM crosstab('SELECT ...') AS ct(...);
```

### citext (case-insensitive text)
```sql
CREATE EXTENSION citext;

CREATE TABLE users (email citext UNIQUE);
INSERT INTO users (email) VALUES ('User@Example.com');
SELECT * FROM users WHERE email = 'user@example.com';   -- match
```

### pg_partman
Particiones automatizadas (usar con tablas huge que crecen por tiempo):
```sql
CREATE EXTENSION pg_partman;
SELECT partman.create_parent('public.logs', 'created_at', 'range', 'monthly');
```

### foreign data wrappers (FDW)
Consultar datos externos como tablas locales:
```sql
CREATE EXTENSION postgres_fdw;   -- otro Postgres
CREATE EXTENSION mysql_fdw;      -- MySQL
CREATE EXTENSION file_fdw;       -- CSV / text files
```

Ejemplo:
```sql
CREATE SERVER remoto_srv FOREIGN DATA WRAPPER postgres_fdw
    OPTIONS (host 'remoto.local', dbname 'app');
CREATE USER MAPPING FOR CURRENT_USER SERVER remoto_srv
    OPTIONS (user 'app_user', password 'x');
IMPORT FOREIGN SCHEMA public FROM SERVER remoto_srv INTO local_schema;

-- Ahora consultás como tabla local
SELECT * FROM local_schema.remote_table;
```

## Crear usuario
```sql
CREATE USER 'app_user'@'10.0.0.%' IDENTIFIED BY 'PassFuerte2026!';

-- Restricción por hosts
CREATE USER 'app_user'@'appserver.local' IDENTIFIED BY 'x';
CREATE USER 'app_user'@'%' IDENTIFIED BY 'x';        -- desde cualquier host (menos seguro)
```

## Grants más usados
```sql
-- Solo lectura sobre una BD
GRANT SELECT ON mi_db.* TO 'readonly'@'10.0.0.%';

-- CRUD sobre una BD
GRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE ON mi_db.* TO 'app_user'@'10.0.0.%';

-- Full sobre una BD
GRANT ALL PRIVILEGES ON mi_db.* TO 'admin_user'@'10.0.0.%';

-- Solo sobre una tabla
GRANT SELECT, INSERT ON mi_db.orders TO 'app'@'10.0.0.%';

-- Solo ciertas columnas
GRANT SELECT (id, name, email) ON mi_db.users TO 'readonly'@'10.0.0.%';

-- Replication
GRANT REPLICATION SLAVE ON *.* TO 'replicator'@'10.0.0.%';
GRANT REPLICATION CLIENT ON *.* TO 'monitor'@'10.0.0.%';

-- Backup
GRANT SELECT, LOCK TABLES, SHOW VIEW, PROCESS ON *.* TO 'backup'@'localhost';

-- Aplicar
FLUSH PRIVILEGES;
```

## Ver permisos
```sql
SHOW GRANTS FOR 'app_user'@'10.0.0.%';

-- Todos los usuarios
SELECT User, Host FROM mysql.user;
```

## Revocar
```sql
REVOKE INSERT ON mi_db.* FROM 'app_user'@'10.0.0.%';
REVOKE ALL PRIVILEGES ON *.* FROM 'app_user'@'10.0.0.%';
```

## Cambiar password
```sql
ALTER USER 'app_user'@'10.0.0.%' IDENTIFIED BY 'NuevaPass2026!';

-- Forzar cambio en próximo login
ALTER USER 'app_user'@'10.0.0.%' PASSWORD EXPIRE;
```

## Eliminar usuario
```sql
DROP USER 'app_user'@'10.0.0.%';
```

## Password policy (MySQL 8.0+)
```sql
-- Validar strength
SELECT VALIDATE_PASSWORD_STRENGTH('mi_password');
-- 100 = strong

-- Config
SET GLOBAL validate_password.policy = MEDIUM;
SET GLOBAL validate_password.length = 12;
SET GLOBAL validate_password.mixed_case_count = 2;
SET GLOBAL validate_password.number_count = 2;
SET GLOBAL validate_password.special_char_count = 2;
```

## Ver usuarios con permisos peligrosos
```sql
SELECT user, host, super_priv, grant_priv
FROM mysql.user
WHERE super_priv = 'Y' OR grant_priv = 'Y';
```

## Least privilege pattern
```sql
-- App = solo CRUD
CREATE USER 'app'@'10.0.%' IDENTIFIED BY 'x';
GRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE ON mi_app.* TO 'app'@'10.0.%';

-- Analytics = solo SELECT
CREATE USER 'analytics'@'10.0.%' IDENTIFIED BY 'x';
GRANT SELECT ON mi_app.* TO 'analytics'@'10.0.%';

-- Admin = para migrations (schema changes)
CREATE USER 'schema_admin'@'localhost' IDENTIFIED BY 'x';
GRANT ALL ON mi_app.* TO 'schema_admin'@'localhost';
-- No PROCESS, no SUPER, no acceso a mysql.*

-- Backup dedicated
CREATE USER 'backup'@'localhost' IDENTIFIED BY 'x';
GRANT SELECT, LOCK TABLES, SHOW VIEW, PROCESS, EVENT, RELOAD ON *.* TO 'backup'@'localhost';
```

## Auditoría
```sql
-- Habilitar audit log (Percona / MariaDB)
SET GLOBAL audit_log_policy = 'ALL';
SET GLOBAL audit_log_format = 'JSON';
```
